WEBVTT

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.970
Seeking out a single ray of light,
hito-suji no hikari wo motome

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:34.210
All I can do is wander on, no matter how far.
hitasura doko made mo tada samayou

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:42.950
As I breathe a sigh not unlike surrender,
akirame ni nita tameiki wo tsuki-nagara

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:52.270
I don't want to fear how I've been hurt, all the time.
kizutsuku koto wo osoretaku nai yo itsu mo

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.650
Set me free now!

00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:01.060
Come on, let it all go, to the far reaches of time,
saa tokihanate subete toki no kanata ni

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:01.080
From that which binds the soul!
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:06.910
tamashii wo shibaru mono wo
From that which binds the soul!

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.200
For my heartbeat!

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.690
Make freedom your weapon,
jiyuu wo buki ni

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:11.760
And you are sure to attain it!
kitto te ni ireru no yo

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.470
kitto te ni ireru no yo
And you are sure to attain it!

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:15.510
The power to believe and dream is there
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:21.590
shinjiru chikara wo yume wo
The power to believe and dream is there

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:21.630
for you to go on living.
ikite yuku tame ni

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.960
ikite yuku tame ni
for you to go on living.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:30.500
Yuji! Yuji!

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:54.400
Code Number 2805, Bullseye Pilot, Marlene Angel...

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:56.660
Having received orders to recover Sleepers,

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:00.730
landed on Earth as a member of Team Gran Seil.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:04.000
Due to activation of the Blue inhabiting the recovery site,

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.740
a Sleeper spontaneously resuscitated.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:09.510
Following the destruction of the spaceport,

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.410
and following the manual, headed toward Baikonur...

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.950
Baikonur Base also destroyed,

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:19.080
one and only recovered Sample sustained severe injuries.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:22.750
What grand results!

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.760
Are there any points that need to be amended?

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:27.090
There are not.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:31.660
Very well. You now have an inquiry with the High Council.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.070
Be sure to answer honestly.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:35.440
High Council?

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.910
First of all, in any case, we commend you for your efforts.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.780
We appreciate the manner in which you worked

00:03:45.850 --> 00:03:49.380
to accomplish your duty to the very end, regardless of the outcome.

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:50.720
However...

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:54.920
It cannot be denied that return was greatly behind schedule!

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.720
Even in the unavoidable situation that your Sleeper had awakened.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:03.740
The greatest problem rests in you letting the Sample take part in battle!

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.000
Code Number 2805, when a problem arises,

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:11.410
it is obvious that the obligation of the soldier is to make contact, yes?

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.640
It was thought there was some kind of accident in the relay facilities.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:19.740
By my judgement at the phase where communications were cut off,

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.410
I recognized that things were now up to the platoon.

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:23.750
In which case,

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:26.760
it's clear that the ultimate orders

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:29.090
were handed down by Platoon Leader Robert, right?

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:32.430
No, in battle at the spaceport, Robert became injured,

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:34.860
and there was concern that it would interfere with his duty,

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:36.700
so he withdrew from leadership of the platoon.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:39.530
Oh? Then there was someone who could fulfill the brilliant Robert's duties

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:43.700
in place of him, was there? Who was that?

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.210
Myself.

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:51.170
You should have known that the matter of highest priority in regards to your duty

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:58.050
rested in the recovery of Sleepers and their prompt transport.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.060
Yes.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:01.320
So then, how is it that you made the reckless decision

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:05.730
to allow the precious Sample to endanger his life?

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.390
That would be...

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:08.900
Answer her.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:13.060
This matter could be construed as a violation of military protocol.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:15.470
The biggest reason was our shortage in the absolute number of pilots.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:18.630
It would be impossible for us to overcome the land overrun by Blue

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:22.080
having lost an Armor Shrike.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.410
That's no reason! Your military training is to that end, isn't it!?

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:28.540
Every contingency is provided for in the manual!

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:31.020
Now, we cannot help but question

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:34.680
your responsibility to carrying out your duty!

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:37.560
Let's change the intent of the question a bit.

00:05:37.630 --> 00:05:45.040
Having the Sleeper in the Armor Shrike - is that something you yourself suggested?

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:49.040
As I remember, he volunteered himself.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:50.370
The Sample did?

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:53.040
Absurd! Such a situation is unanticipated!

00:05:53.110 --> 00:05:55.710
Could being activated due to his early awakening be the cause?

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:58.040
I knew we should have discarded Samples

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:01.050
that were awakened as a result of an accident!

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:04.890
However, the recovery rate of Samples was far lower than estimated!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.390
We can't complain about their condition at the time they are recovered!

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.090
That's outcome-based thinking!

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:14.060
We do not want any accidents during their original state!

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.830
Your opinions are all understandable.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:20.530
However, right now, based on these results,

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:25.070
I wonder if we shouldn't investigate the handling of Samples from here on.

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:28.740
It's obvious! We should move ahead to the next step.

00:06:28.850 --> 00:06:30.440
That should be fine.

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:33.350
I hear his condition is still serious.

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:37.350
We can't afford to just wait until the Sample recovers!

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:39.190
The conditions of preservation for the Sample

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:41.660
should be unrelated to the next step.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:44.350
As far as that is concerned, I have no objection.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:47.020
In that case, let us immediately start preparing...

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.030
How is Yuji?

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:51.330
Is Yuji all right?

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:55.670
Ever since we arrived on the station, I have not received any information.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:57.710
How is he now?

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:02.710
Yuji? You mean the Sample that you recovered?

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:07.720
His becoming injured was my own fault. His progress concerns me.

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:11.380
It is of no matter to you.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.390
B- but...

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:17.390
The inquiry is concluded!

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:20.730
As a result of this inquiry, you have been judged to be unfit...

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.730
- for squad duty.

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:25.430
Starting tomorrow,

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.270
you will transfer to the drill facility and be re-educated from lesson 1!

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:46.560
And here we'd at long last arrived...

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:54.420
Yuji...

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:04.170
"Yuji," huh? Do not take your eye off of 2805 for a while, please.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:53.680
I... I... I want to go into space with you!

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:56.230
It is of no matter to you.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:05.030
This is transport shuttle C-2...

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.500
Beginning preparations to dock at Medical Station...

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:11.340
Yuji...

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:30.060
Code Number 2805, this is not your destination.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:31.360
Return to your seat.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.590
My involvement in drilling starts tomorrow.

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:37.660
I have the right to a final check-up before the drills.

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:41.330
I was not directed to do this.

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:42.340
Just open the door.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.430
- But...
- Open it!

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:32.690
Yuji...

00:10:57.420 --> 00:10:58.400
Yuji!

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:05.010
You're alive! Yuji...

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:06.180
Thank goodness!

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:14.360
Them!

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:18.030
I wonder if we shouldn't investigate the handling of Samples from now on.

00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:20.700
We can't afford to just wait until he recovers...

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:22.360
The conditions of preservation for the Sample

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:26.040
should be unrelated to the next step.

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:33.040
What are they planning to do to Yuji? What's of no matter to me?

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:37.380
No! I'll prove it to them my own way!

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:42.050
Yeah, that nothing I did was wrong...

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:44.060
That what me... and Yuji...

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:46.620
...have done up to now...

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:21.190
The virtual simulation we are about to hold is the same as real combat!

00:12:21.270 --> 00:12:25.100
Those who drop out are to be discarded without mercy! Understood!?

00:12:25.170 --> 00:12:28.630
Code Number 426, take pod number 3!

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:33.070
6945, take pod number 4... 3022, take pod number 5...

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:38.050
Same as real combat? Just what I wanted! I'll show them!

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:42.380
My true abilities as a soldier!

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:46.720
All personnel, saddle up!

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:49.060
If they can see that there is no fault in my ability,

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:51.390
that should prove to them...

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:54.260
...that the actions Yuji and I took were correct!

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:26.760
2805! Your response was too slow! What are you doing!?

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:29.430
Why are you hesitating to fire instantly?

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:32.400
If you had fired while facing the groundling cutting in front of the core,

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:35.030
you would have hit your target!

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:39.570
Your suit's upper left arm has taken damage. 15-point minus.

00:13:39.640 --> 00:13:44.050
Which is more important to you? Groundlings, or your Armor Shrike?

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:47.180
Minus points? Me?

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:07.070
What the hell did the people of Second Earth do to them!?

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:10.670
Marlene, what do you think the people here are, anyhow?

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:13.400
They aren't your tools, you know!

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:15.210
The people left on Earth are already dead...

00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:19.610
is that really true, after all, Marlene!?

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:54.180
You damned fool!

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:55.440
Look out!

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:09.720
Hey, behind you!

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:19.400
This isn't good! Hurry!

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:22.060
Stay with me! Are you okay?

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:24.540
Wasn't this just supposed to be a drill!?

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:30.740
I told you, this was the same as real combat!

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:36.380
2805, he has lost the capacity to fight. Move on to your next action immediately!

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:47.030
Let's go!

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:49.030
2805!

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:52.230
Hey, 2805! Are you listening to me!?

00:16:56.770 --> 00:16:58.140
What do you think?

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:10.050
What are you doing, come on now!

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:15.060
Do you think in this situation you can fight off the Blue's attacks indefinitely!?

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:17.390
Give up on him immediately!

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:19.730
Hurry on forward!

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.820
If you do not achieve your goal within the appointed time,

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:25.730
you too will be disqualified!

00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:31.670
No, this is fine. It's the people above me who don't understand!

00:17:31.780 --> 00:17:37.910
This is the way that I survived through that hell, together with Yuji!

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:01.900
And yet... Dammit!

00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:10.040
Incredible,

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:16.050
at this pace, it's possible she can make the goal in time!

00:18:16.120 --> 00:18:18.710
Do it.

00:18:18.790 --> 00:18:19.720
B- but...

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.660
The drills are not a game!

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:23.560
It is critical for them to perform their duties

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:26.720
as quickly and as thoroughly as possible!

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:31.670
I want her to realize that. Do it now!

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:32.790
Yes, ma'am!

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:53.060
What!?

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:15.440
See to them.

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:27.720
This is Amick Hendar.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:33.260
Yes... Today's data on 2805... I will collect it and submit it within the day...

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:11.260
So, I've returned to the Medical Station again, have I?

00:20:13.770 --> 00:20:15.200
How hectic...

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:22.100
I'm sure it was...

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:40.260
Yuji...

00:20:58.080 --> 00:21:01.610
It can't be... why...?

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:04.280
Yuji!

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:39.880
Although the days when we smiled again and again
hohoemi kasaneta hibi ga

00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:46.010
Have passed away into dreams,
maboroshi ni natte mo

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:55.160
I will surely not lose my way.
watashi wa kitto mayowanai

00:21:55.280 --> 00:22:01.330
To go on to the future,
mirai ni yuku tame ni

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:07.750
To become an adult,
otona ni naru tame ni

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:14.940
I again recall now the memories
mogaite kita omoide wo kokoro de

00:22:15.130 --> 00:22:20.100
twisting in my heart.
ima wa kurikaesu

00:22:20.200 --> 00:22:26.160
I'm living in one time,
hitotsu no toki wo iki

00:22:26.460 --> 00:22:32.440
While choosing two dreams,
futatsu no yume erabi

00:22:33.050 --> 00:22:39.920
And love taught me what it means...
soshite ai ga oshiete kureta yo ne

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:46.780
to cherish someone.
hito wo omou imi

00:22:52.030 --> 00:22:56.290
Something is starting to happen, in a place I do not know of.

00:22:56.370 --> 00:23:00.630
Once my duty is over, it is of no matter to me. I understand that.

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:04.640
However, I can't live like this.

00:23:04.710 --> 00:23:08.300
I traveled with Yuji, I reached this place with Yuji.

00:23:08.380 --> 00:23:13.440
And now, I want to know where Yuji is. That's all I want!
